=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  play firewall/pve9-ufw ---------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: firewall/pve9-ufw$
# web-01.example.net is a Proxmox VE 9 node where origin/main$
# enabled ufw: pve-firewall disabled, ufw active with$
# ENABLED=yes. hardn reads ufw.conf alone and makes no ufw call$
# (decision 7).$
$
# Firewall Configuration #######################################$
$
  [ ] Firewall             Not Configured disabled$
$
  pve-firewall -------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Service              Running$
  [ ] Enabled              No$
   -  Incoming policy      Drop$
   -  SSH (22)             Not filtered$
   -  Web UI (8006)        Not filtered$
  [ ] ufw                  Left on Run ufw disable$
   -  hardn reads pve-firewall and doesn't change it: a wrong$
      rule can cut off the web UI and the cluster.$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter selection [0 or q]: 0$
$
  simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Nothing was applied.$
$

